From: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Subject: KVM: s390: pci: Fix aisb calculation
Patch-mainline: v7.1-rc4
Git-commit: 0cfe660559e857d7c00ab86c73e4510ce069086f
References: bsc#1277451

Description: KVM/s390/pci: Fix resource leaks and cleanup in error paths
Symptom: resource leaks, denial-of-service
Problem: Error paths in interrupt forwarding logic for passthrough PCI devices
         failed to cleanup resources correctly.       
Solution: Fix the logic and handle cleanup appropriately.      
Reproduction:  -

Upstream-Description:

              KVM: s390: pci: Fix aisb calculation

              The current implementation of aisb calculation will erroneously index
              via an unsigned long * as well as multiply by 8B for every 64-bits in
              the offset; only one or the other is required.  This throws off aisb
              calculations once the number of devices exceeds 64, and can result
              in out-of-bounds access as well as failure to indicate summary bits
              associated with those devices in guests.

              Fix this by converting to a physical address before applying the
              offset, as is already done in arch/s390/pci/pci_irq.c.

              Fixes: 3c5a1b6f0a18 ("KVM: s390: pci: provide routines for enabling/disabling interrupt forwarding")
              Signed-off-by: Matthew Rosato <mjrosato@linux.ibm.com>
              Reviewed-by: Niklas Schnelle <schnelle@linux.ibm.com>
              Signed-off-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>


Signed-off-by: Farhan Ali <alifm@linux.ibm.com>
Acked-by: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
---
 arch/s390/kvm/pci.c |    4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
+++ b/arch/s390/kvm/pci.c
@@ -167,7 +167,7 @@ static int kvm_zpci_set_airq(struct zpci
 	fib.fmt0.noi = airq_iv_end(zdev->aibv);
 	fib.fmt0.aibv = virt_to_phys(zdev->aibv->vector);
 	fib.fmt0.aibvo = 0;
-	fib.fmt0.aisb = virt_to_phys(aift->sbv->vector + (zdev->aisb / 64) * 8);
+	fib.fmt0.aisb = virt_to_phys(aift->sbv->vector) + (zdev->aisb / 64) * 8;
 	fib.fmt0.aisbo = zdev->aisb & 63;
 	fib.gd = zdev->gisa;
 
@@ -310,7 +310,7 @@ static int kvm_s390_pci_aif_enable(struc
 
 	/* Update guest FIB for re-issue */
 	fib->fmt0.aisbo = zdev->aisb & 63;
-	fib->fmt0.aisb = virt_to_phys(aift->sbv->vector + (zdev->aisb / 64) * 8);
+	fib->fmt0.aisb = virt_to_phys(aift->sbv->vector) + (zdev->aisb / 64) * 8;
 	fib->fmt0.isc = gisc;
 
 	/* Save some guest fib values in the host for later use */
